--
-- THE TIER'S CENTRAL FACT: the two properties a reservoir engineer uses most,
-- Bo and Rs, are measured by NO single experiment. The differential
-- liberation supplies the shape and is referenced to a residual oil at 60 F;
-- the separator test supplies the level and defines what a stock tank barrel
-- is. Combining them by the Amyx correction is a modelling choice, exact at
-- the bubble point by construction and approximate below it.
-- THE TIER'S SHARPEST RESULTS, both quantified against a measurement rather
-- than asserted: the untuned model comes out 8.894358353620603 API LIGHT,
-- which is worse than a separator test would give and inverts the assumption
-- that a compositional model beats a correlation; and it DECLINES to report a
-- formation volume factor at all, returning null, because its saturation
-- pressure of 2791.100735294379 psia sits ABOVE the 2634.65 psia the
-- laboratory calls reservoir pressure, so on this model the fluid there is
-- two phase and the quantity is undefined. A null with a documented reason is
-- the only honest output and most software returns something.
-- THE CLASSIC ERROR this tier exists to prevent: the report lists ONE
-- separator stage and the stock tank is a flash stage it does not name.
-- Omitting it leaves the tank gas out of the total, inflates the stock tank
-- volume, and nothing fails.
--
